# Velocity Design Audit Rule (V1.0.0)

After any significant page change, output a short compliance audit.

## When to run the audit
- Run when a layout, component style, section structure, CTA treatment, or branding element was added/changed.
- Skip only for tiny edits (typos, whitespace, trivial copy tweaks).

## Required audit format
Use this exact structure:

- `Elementor Content-Only Context`: PASS or FAIL - confirm no global nav/logo/footer shell was added.
- `Scoped Module Architecture`: PASS or FAIL - confirm wrapper scoping and no leaking global selectors.
- `Reference Harmony (Membership Baseline)`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason on stylistic consistency.
- `Identity/Logo`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason.
- `Color System (60-30-10)`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason.
- `Gradients/Pairings`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason.
- `Typography/Alignment`: PASS or FAIL - confirm Khand + ALL CAPS + italicized treatment for main headings/buttons, plus alignment compliance.
- `Grid/Spacing`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason.
- `Assets/Shapes`: PASS or FAIL - one short reason.
- `SEO Structure`: PASS or FAIL - heading hierarchy, semantic sections, crawlable copy.
- `Metadata Handoff`: PASS or FAIL - meta title/description/canonical/OG recommendations provided when needed.
- `Schema Readiness`: PASS or FAIL - relevant schema recommendation included (or not applicable).
- `Overall`: PASS if all categories pass, otherwise FAIL.

## Failure handling
- If any item is FAIL, include a `Fixes` section with minimal, concrete changes needed.
- Prioritize fixes that preserve the current design intent while restoring compliance.
- Do not introduce new colors, spacing systems, or typography outside the standards.
- When applicable, verify compatibility with WordPress/Elementor embedding constraints.
